    "legacy_root": {
      "answer": "[REDACTED] is a typed registry ([REDACTED]-registry/v1) from which plugin.json, marketplace entries, skill/hook/rule deployments, docs, and the workflow and council catalogs are ALL generated. The generator is a pure function: same registry bytes plus generator version 1.0.0 yield 10 byte-identical files across two runs. Every generated file carries a machine-readable provenance header naming registry_id and generator_version. A hand-edit is TAMPERED when bytes differ while registry_entry_sha256 still matches; STALE when the registry entry itself changed. Restore is regenerate. The FIRST construct that is not expressible is an opaque passthrough / untyped blob field copied into generated output: adding that escape hatch reintroduces the drift the generator exists to prevent, so the schema forbids it (additionalProperties false + banned keys).",
